---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **어느 시장이 넓은 작품만 받나.** (`/hard-markets`)
 *
 * ── 왜 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   오늘 「언제」를 여럿 쟀는데 **어디를 먼저 얻고 어디를 마지막에 얻나**는 안 쟀다.
 *   배급 순서를 짜는 사람이 첫째로 묻는 것이다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 ────────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **93곳을 줄세우지 않는다.** 양 끝 다섯씩만 놓고 **왜 다른지**를 옆 칸에 같이 적는다.
 * ⛔ 🔴 **「어렵다」와 「한국 작품을 드물게 트는 곳」을 같은 말로 안 쓴다.**
 *    한국 몫을 나란히 내고, 몫이 비슷한 시장끼리 묶은 표를 **바로 아래** 둔다.
 *    ⭐ 묶어 보면 넓이가 62 → 52 → 46 → 21 로 내려간다. 그 사실을 감추지 않는다.
 *    ⚠ 그래도 둘을 **완전히 갈라내지는 못한다.** 그 한계를 화면에 적는다.
 * ⛔ 작품 이름을 안 낸다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않는다. Riot Production(App 866800) 승인 전이다.
 * ⚠ 수를 손으로 적지 않는다. 전부 `wikitip-hard-markets.json` 에서 읽는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/wikitip-hard-markets.json';

const 띠영어 = {
  '5% 미만': 'Under 5%', '5–8%': '5–8%', '8–12%': '8–12%', '12% 이상': '12% or more',
};
const 한국 = d.narrowToo.find((m) => m.name === 'South Korea');
const 가장넓은쪽 = d.widestOnly[0];

const TITLE = 'Which markets only take the wide Korean titles — and which take the narrow ones too';
const DESC =
  `For each of ${d.marketsMeasured} markets, the median breadth of the Korean titles that reached it. `
  + `On Korea's own chart it is ${한국.medianBreadth}; in ${가장넓은쪽.name} it is `
  + `${가장넓은쪽.medianBreadth}. Most of that gap is how often a market plays Korean titles at all.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.netflix.com/tudum/top10', 'https://www.wikidata.org'],
};

/*
 * 🔴 2026-08-10 04:2x — 여기에 **표를 그리는 함수**를 뒀다가 빌드가 죽었다.
 *   Astro 앞말(`---` 사이)은 **TypeScript 다.** JSX 를 넣을 수 없다.
 *   ⚠ 겉으로 뜬 것은 libuv assertion 이라 원인처럼 안 보였다 —
 *     앞부분을 보니 `hard-markets.astro:46 Expected > but found class` 였다.
 *   ⛔ 「빌드가 죽었다」로 멈추지 않고 **에러 앞부분을 봤다.** 표는 본문에 두 번 쓴다.
 */
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/hard-markets">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{d.question}</p>
  <p class="q">
    Korea's own chart — median breadth <b>{한국.medianBreadth}</b>.
    {' '}{가장넓은쪽.name} — <b>{가장넓은쪽.medianBreadth}</b>.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>The two ends</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Only the widest titles get in</th><th>Median breadth</th>
          <th>Korean share of that chart</th><th>Titles measured</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.widestOnly.map((m) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{m.name}</td>
              <td class="tot">{m.medianBreadth}</td>
              <td>{m.koreanSharePc}%</td>
              <td>{m.koreanTitles}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Narrow titles get in too</th><th>Median breadth</th>
          <th>Korean share of that chart</th><th>Titles measured</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.narrowToo.map((m) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{m.name}</td>
              <td class="tot">{m.medianBreadth}</td>
              <td>{m.koreanSharePc}%</td>
              <td>{m.koreanTitles}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note"><b>{d.unit}</b></p>
    <p class="note">
      <b>{한국.narrowTitlePc}% of the Korean titles that chart in Korea reached five markets or
      fewer.</b> In {가장넓은쪽.name}, not one of its {가장넓은쪽.koreanTitles} did.
    </p>
    <p class="note fine">
      {d.whyNotARanking} {d.marketsMeasured} markets are measured — those with at least{' '}
      {d.marketMinTitles} charting Korean titles.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="warn-box">
    <h2>The right-hand column explains a lot of it</h2>
    <p class="warn">
      A market that rarely plays Korean titles at all will show only the biggest ones — not because
      it is hard to reach, but because there is one Korean slot and the biggest title takes it. That
      is a different statement, and the two are entangled.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Korean share of the chart</th><th>Markets</th>
          <th>Median breadth</th><th>Range within the band</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.byBand.map((b) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{띠영어[b.band]}</td>
              <td>{b.markets}</td>
              <td class="tot">{b.medianBreadth}</td>
              <td>{b.spread}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="q">
      It falls straight down: {d.byBand.map((b) => b.medianBreadth).join(', ')}. The more of a chart
      is Korean, the narrower the titles that get onto it.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      <b>But it is not all of it.</b> Inside the under-5% band — {d.byBand[0].markets} markets that
      all play Korean titles about as rarely as each other — the breadth still ranges across{' '}
      {d.byBand[0].spread} markets' worth. Two countries with the same Korean share can want very
      different titles.
    </p>
    <p class="note fine">
      ⚠ {d.whatCannotBeSeparated}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>How this was counted, and what it cannot say</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Source</b> — {d.source}</li>
      <li><b>Rows read</b> — {d.rowsRead.toLocaleString('en-US')}, across{' '}
        {d.titlesMeasured.toLocaleString('en-US')} Korean titles.</li>
      <li><b>Breadth is a lifetime count</b>, not a simultaneous one — a title that spread to 60
        countries slowly counts the same as one that opened in 60 at once. That difference is
        measured separately at <a href="/time-to-peak">when a title is at its widest</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="warn">{d.cannotAnswer}</p>
    <p class="note">
      <a href="/catalogue-depth">How few titles fill half a market</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/time-to-peak">When a title is at its widest</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/where-it-moved">Where the share went</a> · <a href="/about">How we count</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/hard-markets" />
</WikiTip>

<style>
  .warn-box { border-left: 3px solid #b45309; padding-left: 1rem; }
</style>
